{
  "family": "skeletonMerge",
  "description": "Branch reconciliation over the skeleton witness (Phase 549): the dag/ family's scenario (same writes, same ids, same SHA-256 profile), then `input.heads` reconciled. The base is `input.base` when named, else the heads' common base (the deepest common ancestor: the most ancestors, the larger id on a tie); `commonBase` is always reported, \"\" when there is none, and with no base the verdict is `noBase`. The lanes are Dag.reconcileMany's: the region above the base partitioned into SHARED nodes (held by two or more heads, applied once, first) and each distinct head's EXCLUSIVE delta, in the whole drain's order; every unordered pair of exclusive deltas is checked under the pure footprint of each op (Ops.footprint, no policy); the shared region is replayed from the base's state; each lane is replayed alone from there. The verdict is `merged` with the script (shared, then each lane in the order the heads are named) and the tree it lands on with its sha256, or `interfere` with every conflict (left op, right op, address, shape), or `sharedRejected` with the node, or `lanesRejected` with every lane that does not apply, sorted by head id. Every expectation is computed by calling Core; there is no kitVersion stamp. Slot-granular conflicts (`slotClash`) cannot arise here: a skeleton op has no slot footprint.",
